<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 7.15.1: Analyzing Two Sets of Equations </item>
  <item> 7.15.2: The Vertex Form </item>
  <list>
    <item> 7.15.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 7.15.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.15.3: The Coordinates of the Vertex </item>
  <list>
    <item> 7.15.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 7.15.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 7.15.4: The Graph of a Function in Vertex Form </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in 7.15.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Graphing technology </item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their own device.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for these words and notice their use and meanings. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link>. </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson:</para>
